#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064272 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064115 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/id #uuid "0f4baedc-a28a-5b45-97d7-d7e1196b21c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-6113" :question/problem "Howard, the manager of a sci-fi convention, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the convention, $t$ minutes after the convention has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the convention\n\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the convention\n\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the convention\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of people inside the convention $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}N(t)}{\\textrm{d}t} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in }N}{\\textrm{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, $N'(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of people inside the convention changes $t$ minutes after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of people inside the convention at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\nN'(t) = E(t) - L(t).\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517320 :question-generator/id #uuid "0f0d2bb8-5382-52a4-b4a4-3ac767edc02b" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186064272.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064837 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91bce12a-a0ee-508e-9b44-1a9e82a75aac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) = E(t) + L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063080} {:answer/id #uuid "b02d1fbd-19a0-587f-9cb3-faede4da052a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = E(t) - L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063081} {:answer/id #uuid "e83c99ce-81ce-59b5-aa52-e240f898c1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = E(t) \\cdot L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063082} {:answer/id #uuid "ef02aea9-a9c5-59f2-b08a-0b8813557b4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N^{′}(t) = E(t) + L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063083} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe4eed2-52a7-5fd3-a1c6-cdae319434fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t) = E(t) - L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063084}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec4ed13-bf56-57c0-afef-d9dca073a67b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063079}] :question/id #uuid "a8bc5d1f-a3ab-5829-b912-fad0a50e9612" :question/math-academy-id "q-48707" :question/problem "Susan, the new receptionist of the Smithsonian Museum in Washington DC, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of visitors to the museum $t$ minutes after the museum has opened.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the museum\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the museum\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the museum\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148eb00f-3a9c-5cde-b11e-4aa6e5df5baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336227} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce9ccdf-1421-5fcb-b41e-795e91107452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)={r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336606} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4ac506-d0f2-599b-b8f3-e6dce6983161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336611} {:answer/id #uuid "80a522d2-bd93-5515-9735-bcaf1eb17692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=-{r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337197} {:answer/id #uuid "e3743113-4ad5-561d-af41-cbb9230afbba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=-r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d4ac506-d0f2-599b-b8f3-e6dce6983161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336611} :answer-field/id #uuid "874c5434-9157-538e-be59-176244d35d61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97f8f938-0d50-59f5-922b-f7bea8bb44f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72004" :question/problem "Jason, a biologist, is measuring the growth of bacteria in a Petri dish by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of bacteria in the dish.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bacteria in the dish is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of bacteria inside the dish after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of bacteria is increasing at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $N(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${N}^{′}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "539cfdfe-838f-5f01-80a7-fcde0e816b91" :question/math-academy-id "q-112509" :question/problem "Joseph is measuring the height reached by his lime tree by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in years, since he planted the tree:\n\n- $H(t)$ - The tree's height, in centimeters\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the tree's height is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $H(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $H(t)$ gives the tree's height after $t$ years. Then,\n\n$$\n{H}^{'}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}H(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }H}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${H}^{'}(t)$ gives the rate at which the height of the tree increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $H(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${H}^{'}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef1b856-e606-5faf-bc81-d441b2fbfdf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512128} {:answer/id #uuid "59459bbc-bff1-5a8f-9a50-e6ffa451c3d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)\\cdot L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512306} {:answer/id #uuid "a912d151-5821-56b2-bfc3-6a30d519da07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "N(t)=E(t)+L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512502} {:answer/id #uuid "cafddae2-e99e-570b-af04-9b580b7a3489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)+L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512589} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d31616-58ba-5787-a9be-a1cfe9d0322c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d31616-58ba-5787-a9be-a1cfe9d0322c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512684} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee88502-7069-5e01-a8d0-c684a215ef26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186512740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c00a28ec-ae50-52ff-8f5b-35e535d7e4c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48923" :question/problem "To measure the success of an amusement park, Ed uses the following three functions that model the daily number of visitors to the park $t$ minutes after the park is opened to the public.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of people inside the park\n\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which people enter the park\n\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which people leave the park\n\nWhat is the relationship between the functions above?" :question/worked-solution "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of people inside the park $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of people inside the park changes $t$ minutes after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of people inside the park at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11f79d9f-7e6c-5c8e-9aff-c762fbcfd4b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72109" :question/problem "Ramin, a bricklayer, is monitoring the construction of a wall by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $B(t)$ - the number of bricks in the wall.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of bricks in the wall is increasing.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $B(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $B(t)$ gives the number of bricks inside the wall after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{B}^{'}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}B(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }B}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${B}^{'}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of bricks increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $B(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${B}^{'}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ee469f-3408-5fe2-92e1-b73437f736b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{r(t)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244471} {:answer/id #uuid "3c6ca379-be1f-59bb-b575-764bd123d07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)={r}^{2}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244845} {:answer/id #uuid "3fcf123c-f946-58b3-95ea-c7435a4f1def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244873} {:answer/id #uuid "6d60a78d-cfd5-5840-9657-df2315347309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P(t)={r}^{′}(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245280} {:answer/id #uuid "e067d9ea-1418-5133-aff0-81b214ce0135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=1-r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fcf123c-f946-58b3-95ea-c7435a4f1def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{P}^{′}(t)=r(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244873} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc9aea5-67df-59f8-abb7-e8249f8d9def" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59ff5d13-6b87-5fe2-a8ce-d480b49dc41c" :question/math-academy-id "q-112518" :question/problem "Liam, a farmer, is monitoring the construction of a fence by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $P(t)$ - the number of panels in the fence.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of panels in the fence increases.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $P(t)$ and $r(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $P(t)$ gives the number of panels in the fence after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}P(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }P}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${P}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of panels increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $P(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${P}^{′}(t)=r(t).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa38f112-466c-50e9-ac08-be72b6f53782" :knowledge-point/title "Relating a Derivative to a Rate of Change"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022f3b45-6eba-59cd-ac96-d1dfcb9395b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)+L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244325} {:answer/id #uuid "38f59574-01db-50b0-97d7-bc444b6a4d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244818} {:answer/id #uuid "6aea9487-58e2-53d6-